<title>YUGOSLAVIA: Yugoslav May retail sales rise 6.0 pct vs April.</title>
<headline>Yugoslav May retail sales rise 6.0 pct vs April.</headline>
<dateline>BELGRADE 1997-06-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Statistics Office reported the following economic indicator details.</p>
<p> YUGOSLAV RETAIL SALES	 MAY	   APRIL	  MAY 96</p>
<p> pct change mth/mth	  + 6.0	   - 2.0	  -  1.0</p>
<p> pct change yr/yr	    +18.0	   +23.0	  +125.0</p>
<p>CUMULATIVE FIGURES (JAN TO MAY)</p>
<p> pct change yr/yr	    +19.0	   +31.0	  +121.0</p>
<p>NOTES -- May retail sales were 12 percent above the average for 1996.</p>
<p>Data exclude private sector. Data cover Federal Republic of Yugoslavia, comprising Serbia and Montenegro.</p>
<p>-- Amra Kevic, Belgrade newsroom +381 11 222 4305</p>
</text>
